{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "equiv", "ucas": "it(x: u8, y: u8) = x + y\nthat(x: u8, y: u8) = x - y\nequiv it that", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "equiv", "equal": false, "exhaustive": true, "mismatch_points": 65024, "method": "exhaustive", "counterexample": "x=0, y=1: 1 vs 255"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "it and that differ at 65024 points, e.g. x=0, y=1: 1 vs 255\n"}
{"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "equiv", "ucas": "it(x: u32, y: u32) = (x + y)*(x - y)\nthat(x: u32, y: u32) = x*x - y*y\nequiv it that", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "equiv", "equal": true, "exhaustive": false, "mismatch_points": 0, "method": "algebra"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "derivation", "text": "proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y mod 2^32"}, "files": [], "text": "it and that are equal on the domain of it (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y mod 2^32)\n"}
